  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>A</p>\n<p>The magnetic flux is given by Φ = B * A * cos(α), where α is the angle between the magnetic field vector and the normal to the ring's area. The area is A = πr². The angle of rotation from the horizontal, θ, is equal to α. Solving for α gives arccos(Φ / (B * πr²)) = arccos((2.0 × 10⁻³) / (0.5 * π * (0.05)²)) ≈ 59.4°, which corresponds to option A, 60°.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A ring with a radius of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span> rotates about a horizontal axis in a uniform magnetic field of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.5\\,\\mathrm{T}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the angle of rotation measured from the horizontal when the magnetic flux through the ring is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\,\\mathrm{mWb}\"></span>?</p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60^\\circ\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"75^\\circ\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"85^\\circ\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"89^\\circ\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
